  "summary_en": "This is the definitions section of Nebraska's 2018 statute on automated-driving-system-equipped vehicles (LB989), Neb. Rev. Stat. 60-3301. It defines the terms used in sections 60-3301 to 60-3311. These include automated driving system, driverless-capable vehicle, dynamic driving task, minimal risk condition, operational design domain and on-demand driverless-capable vehicle networks.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines an automated driving system as hardware and software able to perform the entire dynamic driving task on a sustained basis",
   "Defines a driverless-capable vehicle as one that operates without any intervention or supervision by a conventional human driver",
   "Defines a minimal risk condition as a reasonably safe fallback state, such as stopping and turning on the hazard lamps",
   "Defines an on-demand driverless-capable vehicle network for transporting people and goods",
   "Defines the operational design domain (road types, speed range, weather, time of day)"
  ],
